1
00:00:00,852 --> 00:00:03,622
(The Day of the Showdown)

2
00:00:03,852 --> 00:00:05,192
- Nice to see you all. - Nice to see you.

3
00:00:06,052 --> 00:00:08,861
The preview of the First Innocent Moo-Ku Fall Field Day...

4
00:00:08,862 --> 00:00:10,491
aired last week and went viral.

5
00:00:10,492 --> 00:00:11,622
- It did. - Right.

6
00:00:12,162 --> 00:00:14,061
- It did go viral. - People are looking forward to it.

7
00:00:14,062 --> 00:00:15,361
So many people commented that...

8
00:00:15,362 --> 00:00:16,531
they didn't expect to see this many guests...

9
00:00:16,532 --> 00:00:17,561
- Right. - and that...

10
00:00:17,562 --> 00:00:18,571
they were so looking forward to it.

11
00:00:18,572 --> 00:00:20,671
- The expectations are high. - That's right.

12
00:00:20,672 --> 00:00:23,571
The 100m sprint between Sung Hwan and me...

13
00:00:23,572 --> 00:00:25,312
initiated this chain reaction.

14
00:00:26,312 --> 00:00:28,712
(Hyun Moo, do you think you can beat me?)

15
00:00:29,182 --> 00:00:31,011
(It began as Sung Hwan provoked Hyun Moo.)

16
00:00:31,012 --> 00:00:32,352
(Let's do a 100m sprint in front of the MBC building.)

17
00:00:32,982 --> 00:00:36,022
(Hyun Moo and Sung Hwan had a race under the moonlight.)

18
00:00:37,582 --> 00:00:40,152
(These two innocent middle-aged men became intensely competitive.)

19
00:00:41,592 --> 00:00:44,522
(Sung Hwan's tears got Hyun Moo to promise a field day.)

20
00:00:45,862 --> 00:00:46,961
(Then I hope...)

21
00:00:46,962 --> 00:00:48,562
(you can be on my team, MINHO.)

22
00:00:49,662 --> 00:00:52,272
(The embers of their competitiveness turned into a recruiting battle.)

23
00:00:53,032 --> 00:00:55,032
(MINHO)

24
00:00:55,672 --> 00:00:56,941
(To top it off,)

25
00:00:56,942 --> 00:00:58,372
(Old Money came into play.)

26
00:00:59,442 --> 00:01:01,982
(President Jun will pull out all the stops.)

27
00:01:02,812 --> 00:01:06,112
(The day of the field day)

28
00:01:08,012 --> 00:01:09,081
Who's that?

29
00:01:09,082 --> 00:01:11,451
(He trudges along in the rain.)

30
00:01:11,452 --> 00:01:12,952
I could tell by the gait that it was Kian84.

31
00:01:12,992 --> 00:01:14,492
Why are we having a field day in a place like this?

32
00:01:15,662 --> 00:01:18,292
(This is the spot they will assemble for the field day?)

33
00:01:19,092 --> 00:01:20,831
(A curious facial expression)

34
00:01:20,832 --> 00:01:23,332
I was surprised that you called us to a construction site.

35
00:01:25,062 --> 00:01:26,102
Is this the bus?

36
00:01:27,002 --> 00:01:28,271
(The shuttle bus for the Rainbow Club members)

37
00:01:28,272 --> 00:01:30,202
Booking a shuttle bus cost money too.

38
00:01:30,402 --> 00:01:32,311
When we got there, we weren't at a gym.

39
00:01:32,312 --> 00:01:34,471
You just told us to wear a white outfit.

40
00:01:34,472 --> 00:01:35,911
- Right. - We didn't know what was happening.

41
00:01:35,912 --> 00:01:37,381
- I told you to wear a white outfit. - Yes.

42
00:01:37,382 --> 00:01:38,512
There's a reason for that.

43
00:01:39,252 --> 00:01:41,581
(Kian84, dressed in white, gets on the bus for now.)

44
00:01:41,582 --> 00:01:42,721
No one's here yet.

45
00:01:42,722 --> 00:01:44,752
- I was the first one. - You got there quite early.

46
00:01:45,692 --> 00:01:48,762
(He goes all the way to the back as if it was pulling him in.)

47
00:01:49,092 --> 00:01:50,892
(Plopping down)

48
00:01:51,362 --> 00:01:54,632
(Yawning)

49
00:01:55,802 --> 00:01:57,302
Why are we meeting up so early?

50
00:01:57,462 --> 00:01:59,371
Weren't we supposed to meet at 7am?

51
00:01:59,372 --> 00:02:00,902
Right. It was way too early.

52
00:02:02,472 --> 00:02:04,002
How many people are coming?

53
00:02:05,642 --> 00:02:08,372
Two, four, six, eight, ten.

54
00:02:10,542 --> 00:02:11,741
There are 16 seats.

55
00:02:11,742 --> 00:02:13,082
(There's no way 16 people are joining us.)

56
00:02:13,782 --> 00:02:15,581
Oh, hey.

57
00:02:15,582 --> 00:02:17,251
- That's Ji Hyeon's voice. - Hello.

58
00:02:17,252 --> 00:02:19,051
(Ji Hyeon cheerfully walks over.)

59
00:02:19,052 --> 00:02:20,052
My gosh.

60
00:02:20,622 --> 00:02:22,622
- It's been a while. - Hey, it's been a while.

61
00:02:22,822 --> 00:02:25,332
- Why are your hands so chapped? - They're always chapped.

62
00:02:26,362 --> 00:02:27,662
- Have you been well? - Yes.

63
00:02:27,862 --> 00:02:29,531
I've been well. What about you?

64
00:02:29,532 --> 00:02:30,801
I've been well too.

65
00:02:30,802 --> 00:02:32,271
Did you have a nice holiday?

66
00:02:32,272 --> 00:02:33,872
Ji Hyeon is getting friendlier.

67
00:02:34,372 --> 00:02:36,842
By the way, both of us are dressed in white.

68
00:02:37,102 --> 00:02:38,642
Don't we just look like students?

69
00:02:39,272 --> 00:02:41,372
(You're right.)

70
00:02:41,812 --> 00:02:44,312
(A woman dressed in white arrives next.)

71
00:02:44,542 --> 00:02:47,982
- Hello. - Hello.

72
00:02:48,752 --> 00:02:49,881
Nice to meet you.

73
00:02:49,882 --> 00:02:51,221
- That's Dae Ho's other half. - Hello.

74
00:02:51,222 --> 00:02:52,292
(Joking)

75
00:02:52,622 --> 00:02:53,891
- Where would you like to sit? - Hello.

76
00:02:53,892 --> 00:02:55,821
- Sit wherever you want. - Okay.

77
00:02:55,822 --> 00:02:57,391
Since I'm here early, I'll sit in the back too.

78
00:02:57,392 --> 00:02:58,392
Okay.

79
00:02:59,692 --> 00:03:01,531
- Is it your first time meeting her? - Yes.

80
00:03:01,532 --> 00:03:02,562
- It is. - It's our first time, right?

81
00:03:03,302 --> 00:03:05,202
- Aren't you from Mokpo? - Right.

82
00:03:05,502 --> 00:03:06,731
- I'm from Suncheon. - Really?

83
00:03:06,732 --> 00:03:08,072
Yes. Hello. I watched your episodes.

84
00:03:09,002 --> 00:03:11,201
- They hadn't met before that day. - Oh, right.

85
00:03:11,202 --> 00:03:13,112
I bet that was the case for a lot of people.

86
00:03:13,542 --> 00:03:14,912
Is Dae Ho not joining us today?

87
00:03:15,282 --> 00:03:16,312
Is he?

88
00:03:16,682 --> 00:03:18,851
Well, you're close to him. You must know.

89
00:03:18,852 --> 00:03:20,882
- How? We don't stay in touch. - You don't?

90
00:03:21,052 --> 00:03:22,452
- But I think he'll come. - I think he'll come.

91
00:03:22,682 --> 00:03:24,552
(Giggling)

92
00:03:25,722 --> 00:03:26,921
But it's raining today. How will this go?

93
00:03:26,922 --> 00:03:29,692
We were so worried about that. It rained a lot.

94
00:03:30,162 --> 00:03:31,921
A long time ago, even when it rained...

95
00:03:31,922 --> 00:03:33,732
- on a field day like this, - Yes.

96
00:03:33,862 --> 00:03:35,531
people still went through with it, right?

97
00:03:35,532 --> 00:03:36,602
- On our show? - Yes.

98
00:03:36,832 --> 00:03:38,402
No, I mean when you were in school.

99
00:03:38,672 --> 00:03:40,031
- We did even if it rained. - We did even if it rained.

100
00:03:40,032 --> 00:03:41,072
We still went through with it.

101
00:03:41,272 --> 00:03:42,642
We still did it even when it rained.

102
00:03:43,842 --> 00:03:46,442
(It looks like someone has just left his school.)

103
00:03:48,742 --> 00:03:50,711
- My gosh. - Gosh. An after-school program...

104
00:03:50,712 --> 00:03:53,311
- Gosh. No. It's Ju Seung. - My gosh, what's wrong with him?

105
00:03:53,312 --> 00:03:54,352
(Ju Seung shows up in a white taekwondo uniform.)

106
00:03:55,422 --> 00:03:56,482
Where is it?

107
00:03:56,622 --> 00:03:57,882
Wait. That must be it.

108
00:03:59,422 --> 00:04:00,521
Someone's coming.

109
00:04:00,522 --> 00:04:01,892
(Someone else is coming.)

110
00:04:02,422 --> 00:04:04,362
It's Ju Seung.

111
00:04:04,892 --> 00:04:06,191
(He's wearing a taekwondo uniform.)

112
00:04:06,192 --> 00:04:07,692
He's indeed a martial artist.

113
00:04:08,632 --> 00:04:10,461
But you have to understand...

114
00:04:10,462 --> 00:04:12,331
that was probably the only white outfit he had.

115
00:04:12,332 --> 00:04:14,132
- Is that so? - He wears that around his area.

116
00:04:16,002 --> 00:04:17,771
He looked like an elementary school kid.

117
00:04:17,772 --> 00:04:19,411
He could get on the yellow school bus.

118
00:04:19,412 --> 00:04:20,712
Right. The one behind our bus.

119
00:04:22,042 --> 00:04:23,342
- He looks young too. - Right.

120
00:04:24,012 --> 00:04:26,512
- Hello. - Hello. Nice to meet you.

121
00:04:26,812 --> 00:04:27,882
(Intrigued)

122
00:04:28,412 --> 00:04:30,052
Gosh, I ought to make a bold impression.

123
00:04:30,852 --> 00:04:32,021
What bold impression?

124
00:04:32,022 --> 00:04:33,352
You're indeed a martial artist.

125
00:04:34,522 --> 00:04:35,761
I wore this to earn your trust.

126
00:04:35,762 --> 00:04:36,892
(I wore this to earn your trust.)

127
00:04:37,392 --> 00:04:38,462
Is that the bus?

128
00:04:39,062 --> 00:04:40,862
- They're here. - That's it. "Fall Field Day."

129
00:04:42,262 --> 00:04:43,602
The besties are here.

130
00:04:44,032 --> 00:04:45,702
Wait. How many people are joining us?

131
00:04:46,372 --> 00:04:47,472
Hello.

132
00:04:47,602 --> 00:04:49,101
- Hello. - Hello.

133
00:04:49,102 --> 00:04:50,602
- Hello. - Hello.

134
00:04:50,772 --> 00:04:52,212
- You're here. - Hello.

135
00:04:52,642 --> 00:04:53,772
He's the only one who's excited.

136
00:04:54,812 --> 00:04:56,282
- You're here. - You were the first one?

137
00:04:56,342 --> 00:04:57,482
I was the first one.

138
00:04:57,812 --> 00:04:59,252
My gosh.

139
00:04:59,782 --> 00:05:02,051
I haven't woken up this early in a while.

140
00:05:02,052 --> 00:05:03,722
You should try waking up early in the morning.

141
00:05:03,922 --> 00:05:05,082
I can't.

142
00:05:05,422 --> 00:05:07,492
Mr. Jun. Is he not coming?

143
00:05:07,622 --> 00:05:09,262
- I thought you'd be the first one. - Yes.

144
00:05:09,962 --> 00:05:11,021
(About an hour ago)

145
00:05:11,022 --> 00:05:13,431
My gosh. It's nice and scenic.

146
00:05:13,432 --> 00:05:14,892
- It's nice and scenic, right? - Yes.

147
00:05:15,132 --> 00:05:18,262
I'm glad it's not so sunny. A rainy day isn't so bad.

148
00:05:18,602 --> 00:05:19,872
Given the amount of rainfall,

149
00:05:20,032 --> 00:05:21,872
- it won't be hot today. - It's perfect.

150
00:05:22,032 --> 00:05:23,372
It looks like I'll go shirtless today.

151
00:05:23,702 --> 00:05:24,842
My eyes will be traumatized.

152
00:05:27,142 --> 00:05:28,541
My eyes will be traumatized again.

153
00:05:28,542 --> 00:05:30,242
(Hyun Moo gets out of the car as they bicker.)

154
00:05:31,582 --> 00:05:33,712
- You got there before us. - Of course.

155
00:05:35,052 --> 00:05:38,152
- My gosh. Opening the door... - Hey. Why aren't you getting out?

156
00:05:40,522 --> 00:05:41,651
My gosh, this is nice.

157
00:05:41,652 --> 00:05:43,922
- What's that? - It's raining, Hyun Moo.

158
00:05:44,562 --> 00:05:45,861
I'm the one with the hair loss problem.

159
00:05:45,862 --> 00:05:48,561
- You got one only for yourself? - I should watch out for hair loss.

160
00:05:48,562 --> 00:05:49,702
Come on. Seriously.

161
00:05:50,002 --> 00:05:52,401
What is this? Did you prepare all this?

162
00:05:52,402 --> 00:05:53,501
- I prepared all this. - Gosh.

163
00:05:53,502 --> 00:05:55,442
- You're amazing. - You prepared a lot of stuff.

164
00:05:55,602 --> 00:05:57,001
Hyun Moo prepared all that.

165
00:05:57,002 --> 00:05:58,702
- Let's move the ice box first. - Sure.

166
00:05:59,172 --> 00:06:00,611
My gosh. It's so heavy.

167
00:06:00,612 --> 00:06:02,441
- You set up before we got there. - Gosh.

168
00:06:02,442 --> 00:06:04,282
- Yes. - My goodness.

169
00:06:05,812 --> 00:06:07,882
You have to give me a penalty for this.

170
00:06:08,012 --> 00:06:09,421
A penalty is a bad thing.

171
00:06:09,422 --> 00:06:11,052
Is that a bad thing? Anyway...

172
00:06:12,082 --> 00:06:14,252
Why is it so heavy? I...

173
00:06:14,492 --> 00:06:16,491
It looks like you'll use this as an excuse if you lose.

174
00:06:16,492 --> 00:06:18,092
- No. - You'll use this as an excuse.

175
00:06:20,762 --> 00:06:22,061
Gosh, this is nice.

176
00:06:22,062 --> 00:06:23,531
(Anyway, Hyun Moo, this place is great.)

177
00:06:23,532 --> 00:06:24,962
(It is, right?)

178
00:06:26,672 --> 00:06:28,731
After elementary and middle schools...

179
00:06:28,732 --> 00:06:30,401
- Breathe in the morning air. - It's been a while...

180
00:06:30,402 --> 00:06:32,271
since I felt the rain after I graduated.

181
00:06:32,272 --> 00:06:34,111
- That was a pretty big field. - My gosh. How nice.

182
00:06:34,112 --> 00:06:36,182
- This is great. I'm warming up. - My gosh.

183
00:06:36,882 --> 00:06:38,482
I guess the tracks make me feel alive.

184
00:06:38,642 --> 00:06:40,682
- Really? I'll look forward to it. - Yes.

185
00:06:40,782 --> 00:06:42,351
- You can't make excuses today. - You know what?

186
00:06:42,352 --> 00:06:43,782
It feels right to be walking here.

187
00:06:45,182 --> 00:06:47,721
I hired an agency to set this up.

188
00:06:47,722 --> 00:06:49,862
- My gosh, Hyun Moo. - They set this up...

189
00:06:50,022 --> 00:06:51,222
- President Jun. - last night.

190
00:06:52,832 --> 00:06:54,431
- I hired an agency for this. - There.

191
00:06:54,432 --> 00:06:55,832
They set this up the night before.

192
00:06:56,032 --> 00:06:57,132
They set up everything.

193
00:06:57,732 --> 00:06:59,302
You're indeed President Jun.

194
00:06:59,872 --> 00:07:00,901
You go all out when you do something.

195
00:07:00,902 --> 00:07:01,902
Of course.

196
00:07:02,032 --> 00:07:04,102
- We have to install this. - Really?

197
00:07:04,602 --> 00:07:05,712
It's starting to look legit now.

198
00:07:05,842 --> 00:07:07,412
That's the banner. We need that for the field day.

199
00:07:07,912 --> 00:07:10,111
Today must go well for us to have another field day in the future.

200
00:07:10,112 --> 00:07:11,542
- This is the first one. - Hyun Moo.

201
00:07:11,882 --> 00:07:13,051
- I'm sure... - There.

202
00:07:13,052 --> 00:07:14,451
"Innocent Moo-Ku Fall Field Day."

203
00:07:14,452 --> 00:07:15,521
Gosh, this is amazing.

204
00:07:15,522 --> 00:07:17,721
We joked about this, but it came true.

205
00:07:17,722 --> 00:07:18,922
Gosh, I got goosebumps.

206
00:07:19,092 --> 00:07:20,152
It's because it's chilly here.

207
00:07:21,992 --> 00:07:23,521
Let's hang it there. Around here.

208
00:07:23,522 --> 00:07:25,121
- There? Okay. - It's the perfect spot.

209
00:07:25,122 --> 00:07:26,292
- It's perfect. - Give it some tension.

210
00:07:26,792 --> 00:07:27,861
Tie it up.

211
00:07:27,862 --> 00:07:28,932
You're good.

212
00:07:30,032 --> 00:07:31,132
You're good.

213
00:07:31,932 --> 00:07:32,972
Okay. It's done.

214
00:07:33,202 --> 00:07:34,302
Be careful.

215
00:07:35,502 --> 00:07:36,841
- You're good. - You think so?

216
00:07:36,842 --> 00:07:38,602
That's it. You're doing a great job.

217
00:07:38,872 --> 00:07:39,872
Just like that.

218
00:07:39,873 --> 00:07:41,841
- Sung Hwan did all the work. - Right. He and I...

219
00:07:41,842 --> 00:07:43,081
- Right. - are rivals.

220
00:07:43,082 --> 00:07:44,312
He kept bossing me around.

221
00:07:44,542 --> 00:07:45,952
There you go. Excellent.

222
00:07:46,112 --> 00:07:47,382
It looks amazing.

223
00:07:48,212 --> 00:07:49,721
It looks like there's a long history.

224
00:07:49,722 --> 00:07:51,122
- This is great, Hyun Moo. - Yes.

225
00:07:51,552 --> 00:07:53,292
- Hyun Moo. Listen. - Like it's got some heritage.

226
00:07:53,422 --> 00:07:55,561
- We're starting a new tradition. - That's right.

227
00:07:55,562 --> 00:07:56,621
- That's cool. - The first field day.

228
00:07:56,622 --> 00:07:58,861
- I rented a loudspeaker. - Nice, Hyun Moo.

229
00:07:58,862 --> 00:08:01,091
A professional loudspeaker was way too expensive.

230
00:08:01,092 --> 00:08:03,862
- Gosh. Given your case, - I just...

231
00:08:04,102 --> 00:08:05,161
this is quite disappointing.

232
00:08:05,162 --> 00:08:06,272
You mean scale, not case.

233
00:08:06,872 --> 00:08:08,831
Hyun Moo. Just read between the lines.

234
00:08:08,832 --> 00:08:10,141
Don't you know me?

235
00:08:10,142 --> 00:08:11,972
- Gosh. - Yes, this one is expensive too.

236
00:08:12,242 --> 00:08:13,871
- Gosh. Check out the scale of this. - Okay.

237
00:08:13,872 --> 00:08:15,681
(I think we're about ready for the field day.)

238
00:08:15,682 --> 00:08:16,742
All done.

239
00:08:17,042 --> 00:08:19,312
The two of the oldest members set up the event.

240
00:08:20,282 --> 00:08:22,681
- That's the thing about field days. - Right. It's different with ours.

241
00:08:22,682 --> 00:08:23,921
They are harder on the teachers...

242
00:08:23,922 --> 00:08:25,152
- than the students. - Of course.

243
00:08:25,422 --> 00:08:27,421
But two principals came out to set this up.

244
00:08:27,422 --> 00:08:28,921
- A principal and a vice-principal. - A vice-principal.

245
00:08:28,922 --> 00:08:30,362
- We took care of that. - A principal and a vice-principal.

246
00:08:30,592 --> 00:08:32,162
- We're done. - We're done.

247
00:08:32,792 --> 00:08:33,931
Then...

248
00:08:33,932 --> 00:08:35,802
- We can just wait for them to come. - We just wait.

249
00:08:36,062 --> 00:08:37,302
They're coming, right?

250
00:08:38,662 --> 00:08:40,431
Hey. If they don't show up,

251
00:08:40,432 --> 00:08:41,931
we... What are we going to do?

252
00:08:41,932 --> 00:08:43,571
We should just run for a bit and go.

253
00:08:43,572 --> 00:08:44,601
We were worried...

254
00:08:44,602 --> 00:08:45,812
- that you might not come. - Right. It was way too quiet.

255
00:08:46,012 --> 00:08:47,342
We actually considered that.

256
00:08:47,872 --> 00:08:49,942
(You punks)

257
00:08:50,712 --> 00:08:52,142
Hyun Moo, it's raining a lot.

258
00:08:52,812 --> 00:08:54,312
Why aren't they here already? It's making me anxious.

259
00:08:54,452 --> 00:08:55,722
What if Ju Seung is the only one who shows up?

260
00:08:56,422 --> 00:08:58,482
- Why aren't they here already? - What's taking them so long?

261
00:08:58,582 --> 00:09:00,052
Is MINHO scared?

262
00:09:02,122 --> 00:09:04,591
(Meanwhile, someone arrives at the bus.)

263
00:09:04,592 --> 00:09:06,191
- Hello. - Hello.

264
00:09:06,192 --> 00:09:08,031
- Hello. - Hello.

265
00:09:08,032 --> 00:09:09,562
- You're here. - Hello.

266
00:09:09,762 --> 00:09:11,032
- You're here. - Hello.

267
00:09:11,132 --> 00:09:12,471
- There you are. - Hello.

268
00:09:12,472 --> 00:09:13,702
- You're here. - Hello.

269
00:09:14,102 --> 00:09:15,702
My gosh, hello.

270
00:09:16,042 --> 00:09:17,301
My gosh, we all look so white.

271
00:09:17,302 --> 00:09:19,112
- Hello. - Hello.

272
00:09:19,342 --> 00:09:20,512
I'm nervous.

273
00:09:22,442 --> 00:09:23,982
- It's Lee Jung. - Lee Jung.

274
00:09:24,182 --> 00:09:26,012
Lee Jung who said I looked older than my age.

275
00:09:26,852 --> 00:09:29,181
- It's my first field day. - Exactly.

276
00:09:29,182 --> 00:09:30,422
It was her first field day ever.

277
00:09:32,052 --> 00:09:34,592
- Hello. - Hello.

278
00:09:34,692 --> 00:09:36,492
- Hello. - Hello.

279
00:09:36,592 --> 00:09:38,122
- I was quite excited on the bus. - Hello.

280
00:09:38,492 --> 00:09:39,632
People kept coming in.

281
00:09:39,762 --> 00:09:40,792
What?

282
00:09:40,932 --> 00:09:42,702
- Hello. - What's wrong with your hair?

283
00:09:43,732 --> 00:09:45,402
- Hello. - Hi.

284
00:09:46,032 --> 00:09:47,901
You look like a street fighter.

285
00:09:47,902 --> 00:09:49,802
- Your hair... - You do look sharp.

286
00:09:50,172 --> 00:09:51,501
- Like you'll resist the wind. - You sound pretty tough...

287
00:09:51,502 --> 00:09:52,812
in the taekwondo uniform.

288
00:09:54,342 --> 00:09:55,412
You...

289
00:09:57,982 --> 00:09:59,411
(Eating the Shine Muscat)

290
00:09:59,412 --> 00:10:00,512
(Tapping)

291
00:10:01,012 --> 00:10:02,482
Gosh, can I have some?

292
00:10:02,822 --> 00:10:03,952
Thank you.

293
00:10:04,782 --> 00:10:07,122
- I loved that she brought snacks. - Thank you.

294
00:10:07,322 --> 00:10:08,822
It must've been fun on the bus.

295
00:10:11,192 --> 00:10:12,361
Sharing food like that is nice.

296
00:10:12,362 --> 00:10:14,031
Right. That must've been fun.

297
00:10:14,032 --> 00:10:15,291
- You didn't have breakfast, right? - Shine Muscat.

298
00:10:15,292 --> 00:10:16,361
No.

299
00:10:16,362 --> 00:10:17,761
The only thing I got was criticism.

300
00:10:17,762 --> 00:10:18,862
(Joking)

301
00:10:19,632 --> 00:10:22,132
- Do you want the black goat tonic? - Yes. Sounds good.

302
00:10:22,232 --> 00:10:24,041
- You can actually drink this? - I don't know what this is.

303
00:10:24,042 --> 00:10:25,942
- So what's this? - It's the black goat tonic.

304
00:10:26,312 --> 00:10:28,372
- People eat black goats? - Yes.

305
00:10:28,512 --> 00:10:29,541
Really?

306
00:10:29,542 --> 00:10:30,881
- Will this boost my energy? - It looks like a school trip.

307
00:10:30,882 --> 00:10:32,041
It works for me.

308
00:10:32,042 --> 00:10:33,481
- Do you want it? Have it later. - Really?

309
00:10:33,482 --> 00:10:35,312
- Thank you. - It's a precious tonic.

310
00:10:35,552 --> 00:10:36,721
(Gulping down)

311
00:10:36,722 --> 00:10:39,121
I needed to drink that up to boost my energy.

312
00:10:39,122 --> 00:10:40,621
You thoroughly prepared for the field day.

313
00:10:40,622 --> 00:10:41,752
That's great. She does things properly.

314
00:10:42,092 --> 00:10:43,292
Is it good? How does it taste?

315
00:10:44,562 --> 00:10:46,232
- It tastes like a black goat. - It does?

316
00:10:46,792 --> 00:10:47,932
- I guess CODE KUNST isn't coming. - Why isn't CODE KUNST...

317
00:10:48,262 --> 00:10:50,161
- Right. - I don't see CODE KUNST.

318
00:10:50,162 --> 00:10:51,232
Why isn't he here?

319
00:10:52,532 --> 00:10:54,831
- I'm late. - There's always a late student.

320
00:10:54,832 --> 00:10:56,201
You must be punctual.

321
00:10:56,202 --> 00:10:57,372
What? Which bus is it?

322
00:10:57,642 --> 00:10:58,702
There he is.

323
00:11:00,672 --> 00:11:02,911
(I'm sorry I'm late.)

324
00:11:02,912 --> 00:11:05,412
- He's wearing shorts. - He must be so cold!

325
00:11:05,512 --> 00:11:06,712
You're not going to be cold?

326
00:11:07,452 --> 00:11:08,752
Gosh, the bus was full.

327
00:11:09,252 --> 00:11:12,821
President Jun and Sung Hwan are already at the site.

328
00:11:12,822 --> 00:11:15,051
- I see. They're already there. - We can get going now.

329
00:11:15,052 --> 00:11:17,191
- Really? So they weren't late. - All right.

330
00:11:17,192 --> 00:11:18,392
Sir.

331
00:11:19,092 --> 00:11:21,332
- Thank you. - Thank you.

332
00:11:22,162 --> 00:11:23,602
Gosh, this bus is packed.

333
00:11:24,532 --> 00:11:26,302
- There are so many people. - We were all excited.

334
00:11:27,032 --> 00:11:29,572
It's been a while since we had a field day.

335
00:11:29,802 --> 00:11:31,701
The weather was a bit gloomy, but we were all excited...

336
00:11:31,702 --> 00:11:32,872
- I was excited too. - because we were together.

337
00:11:33,212 --> 00:11:34,842
I'm sure they prepared a lot of stuff for today.

338
00:11:35,172 --> 00:11:36,412
We're going pretty far.

339
00:11:36,542 --> 00:11:37,981
The road isn't paved at all.

340
00:11:37,982 --> 00:11:39,281
Gosh, this looks like a tough ride.

341
00:11:39,282 --> 00:11:40,282
(Bumpy)

342
00:11:41,052 --> 00:11:42,621
Hey, how come the bus is going...

343
00:11:42,622 --> 00:11:44,822
- Where are we going? - to a remote place?

344
00:11:45,922 --> 00:11:47,151
(Heading over to a mysterious site)

345
00:11:47,152 --> 00:11:48,851
We had been on the road for a while,

346
00:11:48,852 --> 00:11:50,592
- but we couldn't see the field. - We couldn't. Look.

347
00:11:50,692 --> 00:11:51,862
You're right.

348
00:11:51,962 --> 00:11:53,431
Where on earth are we?

349
00:11:53,432 --> 00:11:55,661
- You guys look like a cult group. - Right, sort of.

350
00:11:55,662 --> 00:11:56,762
You were all dressed in white.

351
00:11:57,362 --> 00:11:59,731
Usually, those excited characters...

352
00:11:59,732 --> 00:12:01,101
- end up dying first. - Right.

353
00:12:01,102 --> 00:12:02,431
That's a great theme...

354
00:12:02,432 --> 00:12:03,842
- for OTT shows. - Right.

355
00:12:04,842 --> 00:12:07,242
("Innocent Moo-Ku Field Day")

356
00:12:10,182 --> 00:12:11,542
Why am I seeing barbed-wire fences?

357
00:12:12,342 --> 00:12:13,412
- What? - Wait.

358
00:12:15,822 --> 00:12:16,982
Everyone is terrified.

359
00:12:17,352 --> 00:12:18,852
- Right. - It was scary.

360
00:12:20,692 --> 00:12:22,491
Gosh, we're here!

361
00:12:22,492 --> 00:12:24,191
Wait, look. They're doing something.

362
00:12:24,192 --> 00:12:25,692
- What are they doing? - Look.

363
00:12:26,162 --> 00:12:27,432
- What are they doing? - What?

364
00:12:30,032 --> 00:12:32,131
(They look like tiny dots in the air.)

365
00:12:32,132 --> 00:12:34,601
- It's raining a lot. - It's raining.

366
00:12:34,602 --> 00:12:35,602
Take it.

367
00:12:36,472 --> 00:12:37,602
Let's go!

368
00:12:37,872 --> 00:12:38,901
(It's pouring.)

369
00:12:38,902 --> 00:12:40,612
(It's raining like cats and dogs.)

370
00:12:40,742 --> 00:12:41,812
Come on.

371
00:12:42,542 --> 00:12:43,781
This is like the opening event...

372
00:12:43,782 --> 00:12:44,982
of a slow pork backbone stew restaurant.

373
00:12:45,542 --> 00:12:47,911
Welcome! We've got pork backbone stew!

374
00:12:47,912 --> 00:12:49,052
Hello.

375
00:12:50,352 --> 00:12:51,882
(The bus pulls in from afar.)

376
00:12:52,892 --> 00:12:57,292
(They don't spare their body to welcome the group.)

377
00:13:02,332 --> 00:13:03,601
When I perform in the countryside,

378
00:13:03,602 --> 00:13:04,832
I see a lot of old people dancing like them.

379
00:13:05,632 --> 00:13:07,201
(Fascinated)

380
00:13:07,202 --> 00:13:08,302
What are they doing?

381
00:13:09,242 --> 00:13:12,042
- Welcome. - Welcome!

382
00:13:12,842 --> 00:13:14,941
We wanted to get the party started before you arrived.

383
00:13:14,942 --> 00:13:16,381
We danced for 30 minutes.

384
00:13:16,382 --> 00:13:17,482
For 30 minutes?

385
00:13:18,342 --> 00:13:20,381
- No wonder why you were tired. - Exactly.

386
00:13:20,382 --> 00:13:23,051
We turned on the music and danced for you guys.

387
00:13:23,052 --> 00:13:24,621
- We were confused, though. - The music?

388
00:13:24,622 --> 00:13:26,422
- We were so far away. - We couldn't hear the music at all.

389
00:13:26,992 --> 00:13:29,291
So you didn't hear the music on the bus?

390
00:13:29,292 --> 00:13:30,521
We couldn't hear the music.

391
00:13:30,522 --> 00:13:31,791
- We were confused. - We thought, "What are they doing?"

392
00:13:31,792 --> 00:13:34,562
We maxed out the volume. But you couldn't hear anything.

393
00:13:37,032 --> 00:13:38,132
See? It was quiet.

394
00:13:38,632 --> 00:13:40,831
The First... What does it say over there?

395
00:13:40,832 --> 00:13:41,931
Moo-Ku...

396
00:13:41,932 --> 00:13:42,972
(Flapping)

397
00:13:43,002 --> 00:13:44,801
We were wondering what you were doing when we got off.

398
00:13:44,802 --> 00:13:46,641
From afar, we look like crazy weirdos.

399
00:13:46,642 --> 00:13:47,642
(Suspicious men in the rain)

400
00:13:49,942 --> 00:13:51,942
They're over there.

401
00:13:52,812 --> 00:13:54,782
What are they doing over there?

402
00:13:54,882 --> 00:13:56,022
They're dancing.

403
00:13:56,422 --> 00:13:57,522
What's this?

404
00:13:57,582 --> 00:13:59,182
Welcome.

405
00:13:59,522 --> 00:14:00,652
Welcome.

406
00:14:01,992 --> 00:14:04,521
- Come on. - They're surely trying hard.

407
00:14:04,522 --> 00:14:05,791
They look like the drunk guys you'd see...

408
00:14:05,792 --> 00:14:07,032
- in the neighborhood. - Right.

409
00:14:08,032 --> 00:14:09,191
(Panting)

410
00:14:09,192 --> 00:14:10,561
They used up all of their energy.

411
00:14:10,562 --> 00:14:12,162
It's okay. We had fun.

412
00:14:12,362 --> 00:14:13,531
What crosses your mind...

413
00:14:13,532 --> 00:14:14,701
- when you see that kind of dance? - Come on.

414
00:14:14,702 --> 00:14:16,871
You'll pass out at noon if you keep that up.

415
00:14:16,872 --> 00:14:18,271
You'll get tired early.

416
00:14:18,272 --> 00:14:19,542
(The organizers are brimming with enthusiasm.)

417
00:14:19,842 --> 00:14:21,641
- Okay. Ja Yeon. - Hello.

418
00:14:21,642 --> 00:14:23,441
- That's a big group indeed. - Hello.

419
00:14:23,442 --> 00:14:24,681
Park Ji Hyeon!

420
00:14:24,682 --> 00:14:26,451
Where should we put our bags?

421
00:14:26,452 --> 00:14:27,452
Over here.

422
00:14:28,412 --> 00:14:30,282
Gosh, I know you're busy. But thanks for coming.

423
00:14:30,722 --> 00:14:31,822
Thank you for having me.

424
00:14:31,882 --> 00:14:33,121
You lost weight.

425
00:14:33,122 --> 00:14:34,392
- You think so? - Yes.

426
00:14:34,652 --> 00:14:35,691
But you gained weight.

427
00:14:35,692 --> 00:14:36,822
(Joking)

428
00:14:37,522 --> 00:14:40,162
It felt like going to an uncle's house.

429
00:14:40,662 --> 00:14:42,831
Right. Hadn't it been a while since we all got together?

430
00:14:42,832 --> 00:14:43,961
Right.

431
00:14:43,962 --> 00:14:45,661
It was the first time we had this many people.

432
00:14:45,662 --> 00:14:47,232
- It was the 1st time. - It was the 1st time. Right.

433
00:14:47,702 --> 00:14:49,641
- The 1st time in 10 years. - We usually met in small groups.

434
00:14:49,642 --> 00:14:51,002
- It's suddenly not raining anymore. - It stopped raining.

435
00:14:51,372 --> 00:14:53,471
It stopped raining as soon as you guys arrived.

436
00:14:53,472 --> 00:14:54,541
It rained a lot...

437
00:14:54,542 --> 00:14:55,612
- when we were setting up. - Right.

438
00:14:57,112 --> 00:14:59,242
No one except for MINHO seems excited.

439
00:15:00,112 --> 00:15:03,022
MINHO looks like the Joker. He keeps smiling.

440
00:15:03,952 --> 00:15:05,081
It's called the Innocent Moo-Ku Field Day.

441
00:15:05,082 --> 00:15:07,822
So we'll divide into Teams Moo and Ku. Okay?

442
00:15:08,252 --> 00:15:09,321
I'll join Team MINHO.

443
00:15:09,322 --> 00:15:10,861
- Me too. - I'll join Team MINHO.

444
00:15:10,862 --> 00:15:11,891
- Me too. - Me too.

445
00:15:11,892 --> 00:15:13,362
- I'll join Team MINHO. - Me too.

446
00:15:13,592 --> 00:15:14,731
I'll join Team MINHO too.

447
00:15:14,732 --> 00:15:16,861
(Captain Ku will join Team MINHO too.)

448
00:15:16,862 --> 00:15:17,931
I'll join Team MINHO too.

449
00:15:17,932 --> 00:15:19,771
- You don't know what we're playing. - No.

450
00:15:19,772 --> 00:15:20,802
(Pulling in)

451
00:15:20,932 --> 00:15:22,172
- What's going on? - What?

452
00:15:22,532 --> 00:15:23,572
What is that?

453
00:15:24,242 --> 00:15:25,972
- What's going on? - What is this?

454
00:15:29,382 --> 00:15:30,712
Ko Kang Yong is here.

455
00:15:30,912 --> 00:15:31,912
What?

456
00:15:32,782 --> 00:15:33,911
- For real? - Really?

457
00:15:33,912 --> 00:15:34,952
- This is crazy. - Hey.

458
00:15:35,182 --> 00:15:36,321
- Hello. - Hello.

459
00:15:36,322 --> 00:15:37,481
- Hello. - He came in a suit.

460
00:15:37,482 --> 00:15:39,952
- He's an MBC employee. - He's got a name tag too.

461
00:15:40,052 --> 00:15:41,891
- A fancy announcer for our event. - Nice to see you.

462
00:15:41,892 --> 00:15:42,921
- Gosh. - Oh, my.

463
00:15:42,922 --> 00:15:45,121
- On behalf of MBC, - Yes.

464
00:15:45,122 --> 00:15:46,662
I brought presents.

465
00:15:46,932 --> 00:15:50,462
The CEO of MBC is personally providing you with these presents.

466
00:15:50,532 --> 00:15:52,331
Everyone, let's give it up for him!

467
00:15:52,332 --> 00:15:53,371
He knows how to run a party.

468
00:15:53,372 --> 00:15:55,472
I should work hard today. There are home appliances!

469
00:15:55,572 --> 00:15:56,841
Everyone, look over there.

470
00:15:56,842 --> 00:15:58,572
There's an ambulance on standby.

471
00:15:59,372 --> 00:16:01,242
- We got a bigger one than idols. - Exactly.

472
00:16:01,512 --> 00:16:03,581
- We're much older than them. - Of course.

473
00:16:03,582 --> 00:16:06,151
All right. Let's move the prizes Kang Yong brought.

474
00:16:06,152 --> 00:16:07,152
(Swarming over to move the prizes)

475
00:16:07,153 --> 00:16:08,452
Gosh, what's this?

476
00:16:08,682 --> 00:16:12,022
My goodness! These are home appliances!

477
00:16:12,222 --> 00:16:13,851
- These are home appliance boxes! - Gosh.

478
00:16:13,852 --> 00:16:16,161
Seeing fancy prizes definitely got us excited.

479
00:16:16,162 --> 00:16:17,891
- Lame prizes can't motivate us. - Exactly.

480
00:16:17,892 --> 00:16:19,062
- Right. - Yes.

481
00:16:19,562 --> 00:16:21,392
Let's stack them up neatly here.

482
00:16:22,802 --> 00:16:24,601
My gosh. This is amazing.

483
00:16:24,602 --> 00:16:25,631
- A Dyson? - It's a Dyson?

484
00:16:25,632 --> 00:16:27,471
Of course. We ought to use tools.

485
00:16:27,472 --> 00:16:29,171
Give them to me. Come down and help us here.

486
00:16:29,172 --> 00:16:30,472
Let's go.

487
00:16:30,672 --> 00:16:32,571
- Look how strong he is. - Put the rice sacks on the cart.

488
00:16:32,572 --> 00:16:34,972
Just put the sacks on the cart!

489
00:16:35,172 --> 00:16:36,641
We've got a cart!

490
00:16:36,642 --> 00:16:38,311
- He could ruin his shoulders. - I should do lunges.

491
00:16:38,312 --> 00:16:39,911
Look. He's doing squats too.

492
00:16:39,912 --> 00:16:41,351
- I told him to put them on a cart. - I mean, lunges.

493
00:16:41,352 --> 00:16:43,682
- My gosh. - There he goes again.

494
00:16:43,752 --> 00:16:45,051
In case it ruins your outfit.

495
00:16:45,052 --> 00:16:46,752
- Why is he wasting his energy? - Why?

496
00:16:47,252 --> 00:16:50,022
This is how people give out their holiday presents.

497
00:16:50,122 --> 00:16:51,161
Really?

498
00:16:51,162 --> 00:16:52,861
- President Jun. - Yes.

499
00:16:52,862 --> 00:16:55,862
Okay, I got it. I'll introduce them. Give me a second.

500
00:16:55,962 --> 00:16:57,132
This is mine.

501
00:16:57,902 --> 00:17:00,331
- You should get a haircut. - Kang Yong prepared everything...

502
00:17:00,332 --> 00:17:02,131
for our event. Thank you. How do I put this on?

503
00:17:02,132 --> 00:17:03,371
- What's that? - What is it?

504
00:17:03,372 --> 00:17:04,671
- They don't listen. - Is he going to sing?

505
00:17:04,672 --> 00:17:05,741
This will be a long event.

506
00:17:05,742 --> 00:17:06,872
- Protect your voice. - There are numbers on it.

507
00:17:07,112 --> 00:17:08,641
There were so many people.

508
00:17:08,642 --> 00:17:10,541
Our teachers used to call out, "Attention."

509
00:17:10,542 --> 00:17:11,542
- I could understand why. - Right.

510
00:17:11,543 --> 00:17:13,382
You guys didn't listen to me at all.

511
00:17:13,752 --> 00:17:16,852
This is great. Now, we're talking. This hits the spot.

512
00:17:17,552 --> 00:17:19,851
Okay. From now on, I'm going to explain some things.

513
00:17:19,852 --> 00:17:21,291
- What? - We don't want to buy pearl cream.

514
00:17:21,292 --> 00:17:23,361
I don't want to buy latex mattresses.

515
00:17:23,362 --> 00:17:24,761
- We don't want to buy gemstones. - No.

516
00:17:24,762 --> 00:17:28,292
All right. I'll introduce the prizes for the winning team.

517
00:17:28,492 --> 00:17:32,331
