00:59:42,748 --> 00:59:44,417
- We need to put our legs down. - Okay.

1787
00:59:44,418 --> 00:59:46,788
We told you guys the day before.

1788
00:59:47,158 --> 00:59:48,558
- We told you guys to pack lunch. - Yes.

1789
00:59:48,728 --> 00:59:50,888
I woke up at the crack of dawn and packed lunch.

1790
00:59:50,988 --> 00:59:53,498
- Okay. - Okay.

1791
00:59:53,998 --> 00:59:55,967
Let's eat packed lunch first.

1792
00:59:55,968 --> 00:59:57,868
(Shall we eat packed lunch?)

1793
00:59:59,798 --> 01:00:01,197
- Oh, my. - I was shocked.

1794
01:00:01,198 --> 01:00:03,367
- I packed so many items. - Na Rae, seriously.

1795
01:00:03,368 --> 01:00:04,767
It was nothing big.

1796
01:00:04,768 --> 01:00:06,507
It's nothing big.

1797
01:00:06,508 --> 01:00:07,838
Well done. I can tell that it's nothing big.

1798
01:00:08,378 --> 01:00:10,147
Are you sure you didn't pack food as if your life depended on it?

1799
01:00:10,148 --> 01:00:11,917
- No. - I wanted to share with everyone.

1800
01:00:11,918 --> 01:00:13,248
That's right. It was so nice.

1801
01:00:14,578 --> 01:00:16,988
- Look at KEY. - Look at his packed lunch.

1802
01:00:17,218 --> 01:00:18,717
(KEY appears with a big bag.)

1803
01:00:18,718 --> 01:00:19,958
It's so big.

1804
01:00:20,188 --> 01:00:21,787
Why are the two of them competing? Hold on a second.

1805
01:00:21,788 --> 01:00:23,527
- It's a match. - Park Na Rae versus KEY.

1806
01:00:23,528 --> 01:00:25,187
- We won't need anything else. - This is incredible.

1807
01:00:25,188 --> 01:00:27,258
Are Na Rae and KEY having a match?

1808
01:00:27,598 --> 01:00:29,397
We won't need to take out our food.

1809
01:00:29,398 --> 01:00:31,497
There's a rival company.

1810
01:00:31,498 --> 01:00:33,197
- Two catering chefs showed up. - That's right.

1811
01:00:33,198 --> 01:00:34,337
Exactly.

1812
01:00:34,338 --> 01:00:36,237
He's from Gyeongsang Province, and I'm from Jeolla Province.

1813
01:00:36,238 --> 01:00:37,737
- Gyeongsang Province... - That's right.

1814
01:00:37,738 --> 01:00:39,978
and Jeolla Province. Is this "Korean Food War?"

1815
01:00:40,278 --> 01:00:42,147
- It's a match between provinces. - Yes.

1816
01:00:42,148 --> 01:00:43,907
There were two catering chefs.

1817
01:00:43,908 --> 01:00:46,547
- That's the most important. - I agree.

1818
01:00:46,548 --> 01:00:48,817
In ten years, you won't remember the games.

1819
01:00:48,818 --> 01:00:49,947
You'll only remember the food.

1820
01:00:49,948 --> 01:00:51,387
- You'll remember what you ate. - I agree. That's a memory.

1821
01:00:51,388 --> 01:00:53,187
That's the actual highlight.

1822
01:00:53,188 --> 01:00:54,188
I agree.

1823
01:00:54,189 --> 01:00:55,987
Who remembers the rankings in the sprint?

1824
01:00:55,988 --> 01:00:57,557
- No one. - You just remember...

1825
01:00:57,558 --> 01:00:58,727
- your mom's tasty gimbap. - That's right.

1826
01:00:58,728 --> 01:01:00,827
- He has a point. - That's right.

1827
01:01:00,828 --> 01:01:02,198
- You remember the menu. - That's right.

1828
01:01:02,328 --> 01:01:03,967
- Park Na Rae, what did you bring? - What?

1829
01:01:03,968 --> 01:01:05,268
Park Na Rae, what did you bring?

1830
01:01:05,568 --> 01:01:06,898
He's wary.

1831
01:01:07,468 --> 01:01:09,607
As for me...

1832
01:01:09,608 --> 01:01:11,467
- You brought a cutting board. - Why is there a cutting board?

1833
01:01:11,468 --> 01:01:13,237
How many kimchi containers did you bring?

1834
01:01:13,238 --> 01:01:14,707
Hey, she brought a cutting board.

1835
01:01:14,708 --> 01:01:16,048
- No way. - I was a bit wary.

1836
01:01:16,508 --> 01:01:18,777
To KEY, this is the 100m sprint.

1837
01:01:18,778 --> 01:01:19,848
That's right.

1838
01:01:20,548 --> 01:01:22,518
(The Lunch Battle of Their Own)

1839
01:01:22,588 --> 01:01:25,688
Who brings a cutting board to a field day?

1840
01:01:26,118 --> 01:01:27,988
It's just like the springboard.

1841
01:01:29,988 --> 01:01:31,758
- Well, - Yes?

1842
01:01:32,258 --> 01:01:35,667
I prepared some cold meat.

1843
01:01:35,668 --> 01:01:38,128
(I prepared some cold meat.)

1844
01:01:38,328 --> 01:01:40,398
The color shows how well it's cooked.

1845
01:01:40,698 --> 01:01:41,868
- It's cooked well, isn't it? - Yes.

1846
01:01:42,108 --> 01:01:43,137
It's cooked to perfection.

1847
01:01:43,138 --> 01:01:44,938
There's cuttlefish with vinegar dressing as well.

1848
01:01:45,108 --> 01:01:46,638
I followed my mom's recipe.

1849
01:01:47,478 --> 01:01:48,848
- The Jeolla Province style. - It looks amazing.

1850
01:01:49,048 --> 01:01:51,778
I went all around Noryangjin for that.

1851
01:01:53,548 --> 01:01:54,677
Have some of the fried tofu rice balls.

1852
01:01:54,678 --> 01:01:56,547
(Generous Na Rae even shares fried tofu rice balls.)

1853
01:01:56,548 --> 01:01:57,587
Give them a try.

1854
01:01:57,588 --> 01:02:00,118
I've never seen fried tofu rice balls that plump.

1855
01:02:00,358 --> 01:02:01,788
He packs this much just for a taste?

1856
01:02:01,918 --> 01:02:02,928
Hey!

1857
01:02:03,388 --> 01:02:05,528
Na Rae is just like Auntie Omakase.

1858
01:02:05,758 --> 01:02:06,758
Na Rae Omakase.

1859
01:02:07,498 --> 01:02:08,727
Did you have time for this?

1860
01:02:08,728 --> 01:02:09,967
Who packs cuttlefish with vinegar dressing...

1861
01:02:09,968 --> 01:02:10,998
to a field day?

1862
01:02:11,898 --> 01:02:13,667
There might be leftovers.

1863
01:02:13,668 --> 01:02:15,708
Are you serious, Kim Ki Bum?

1864
01:02:16,238 --> 01:02:17,438
I brought some for a taste as well.

1865
01:02:17,508 --> 01:02:18,707
What are those blue crabs?

1866
01:02:18,708 --> 01:02:19,977
- What? - Look at him.

1867
01:02:19,978 --> 01:02:22,407
- Blue crabs? - We won't need more food.

1868
01:02:22,408 --> 01:02:23,708
It's for everyone to have a taste.

1869
01:02:24,278 --> 01:02:25,918
- He's open-handed as well. - Gosh.

1870
01:02:26,578 --> 01:02:27,817
He's open-handed as well.

1871
01:02:27,818 --> 01:02:28,888
What is this?

1872
01:02:29,518 --> 01:02:32,518
I prepared braised crabs with my grandmother's recipe.

1873
01:02:33,118 --> 01:02:34,218
Braised crabs?

1874
01:02:35,728 --> 01:02:38,758
(KEY especially loved his grandmother's braised crabs.)

1875
01:02:39,058 --> 01:02:41,028
- We were all curious about it. - Right.

1876
01:02:41,428 --> 01:02:42,928
Who brings crabs to a field day?

1877
01:02:44,298 --> 01:02:46,368
- Gosh. - It was a first for me as well.

1878
01:02:46,768 --> 01:02:48,537
They're in season right now.

1879
01:02:48,538 --> 01:02:49,807
- Right. They were delicious. - Right.

1880
01:02:49,808 --> 01:02:51,208
The crabs were huge as well.

1881
01:02:52,178 --> 01:02:53,277
So you brought all of this...

1882
01:02:53,278 --> 01:02:54,378
- to share with everyone. - Right.

1883
01:02:54,578 --> 01:02:57,577
I ordered 5kg of crabs as I didn't know how many would be here.

1884
01:02:57,578 --> 01:02:58,777
- What? - You ordered 5kg of crabs.

1885
01:02:58,778 --> 01:03:02,318
- He cooked for four hours. - Right.

1886
01:03:02,448 --> 01:03:03,648
Blue crabs are in season right now.

1887
01:03:03,748 --> 01:03:05,788
MINHO doesn't know how to cook.

1888
01:03:06,158 --> 01:03:07,857
- You cooked for him as well? - I prepared rice for him as well.

1889
01:03:07,858 --> 01:03:09,288
I made grilled rice balls...

1890
01:03:09,758 --> 01:03:11,758
- and rolled omelets. - They're even grilled.

1891
01:03:12,158 --> 01:03:13,258
I brought other dishes as well.

1892
01:03:13,328 --> 01:03:14,657
(Amazed)

1893
01:03:14,658 --> 01:03:15,727
He's a great friend.

1894
01:03:15,728 --> 01:03:16,927
Ki Bum is so nice.

1895
01:03:16,928 --> 01:03:17,928
(Ki Bum is so nice.)

1896
01:03:18,738 --> 01:03:19,868
Pass it to each person.

1897
01:03:20,598 --> 01:03:21,937
It's one crab per person.

1898
01:03:21,938 --> 01:03:23,537
- It's one crab per person? - Yes.

1899
01:03:23,538 --> 01:03:24,968
- Really? - Of course.

1900
01:03:25,168 --> 01:03:26,877
- Each person gets one crab. - Right.

1901
01:03:26,878 --> 01:03:28,778
- He wants to bring some home. - Go ahead and take some home.

1902
01:03:29,508 --> 01:03:30,677
- It's enough for everyone. - Gosh.

1903
01:03:30,678 --> 01:03:33,447
Packed lunches should be packed like Kian84.

1904
01:03:33,448 --> 01:03:35,278
- What did he bring? - He brought it just for himself.

1905
01:03:36,518 --> 01:03:37,648
That's how it should be.

1906
01:03:38,488 --> 01:03:39,617
He brought just enough for himself.

1907
01:03:39,618 --> 01:03:40,917
It's fried rice.

1908
01:03:40,918 --> 01:03:42,628
(Kian84's seed fried rice)

1909
01:03:42,758 --> 01:03:44,257
- You promised me a bite. - What?

1910
01:03:44,258 --> 01:03:45,728
- You promised me a bite. - Sure.

1911
01:03:46,298 --> 01:03:47,327
(He happened to promise him a bite of his seed fried rice.)

1912
01:03:47,328 --> 01:03:49,527
All right. Let's use this time...

1913
01:03:49,528 --> 01:03:51,668
to reveal what each of us brought.

1914
01:03:51,828 --> 01:03:53,467
(Blinking)

1915
01:03:53,468 --> 01:03:55,337
- Where is Dae Ho hiding? - I'm here.

1916
01:03:55,338 --> 01:03:56,668
Show us what you've brought.

1917
01:03:57,668 --> 01:03:58,907
His bag was switched.

1918
01:03:58,908 --> 01:03:59,977
Gosh!

1919
01:03:59,978 --> 01:04:01,107
It's bibimbap.

1920
01:04:01,108 --> 01:04:02,208
What's wrong with him?

1921
01:04:04,848 --> 01:04:06,048
Gosh, that looks awful.

1922
01:04:07,618 --> 01:04:09,617
I'm sorry, Dae Ho!

1923
01:04:09,618 --> 01:04:12,518
(Dae Ho's strange bag of lunch)

1924
01:04:14,458 --> 01:04:16,328
(Gosh!)

1925
01:04:17,858 --> 01:04:19,258
It was shocking.

1926
01:04:19,798 --> 01:04:21,257
- Gosh! - Gosh!

1927
01:04:21,258 --> 01:04:22,268
(Feeling embarrassed)

1928
01:04:23,498 --> 01:04:25,168
- Bye, Dae Ho! - Bye!

1929
01:04:26,368 --> 01:04:27,438
Gosh.

1930
01:04:27,698 --> 01:04:28,767
Is it sold like that?

1931
01:04:28,768 --> 01:04:30,267
- I made it at home. - You made it at home?

1932
01:04:30,268 --> 01:04:31,567
- Well, - It would never be sold like that.

1933
01:04:31,568 --> 01:04:32,807
I flew back in the morning after a shoot abroad.

1934
01:04:32,808 --> 01:04:34,077
What's the name of the dish?

1935
01:04:34,078 --> 01:04:35,878
- It's bibimbap. - It's chow.

1936
01:04:36,248 --> 01:04:37,308
Chow?

1937
01:04:37,478 --> 01:04:39,618
It's squeezed out to be eaten after cutting the end with scissors.

1938
01:04:40,348 --> 01:04:41,777
- It's squeezed out? - It looks stunning.

1939
01:04:41,778 --> 01:04:43,517
It should be torn up with the teeth, to be precise.

1940
01:04:43,518 --> 01:04:46,417
- So it's a forcing bag? - I will ask for some side dishes.

1941
01:04:46,418 --> 01:04:48,318
We won't ask for any of yours, Dae Ho.

1942
01:04:48,458 --> 01:04:49,488
You should have some.

1943
01:04:50,488 --> 01:04:51,728
What about you, Lee Jung?

1944
01:04:51,928 --> 01:04:53,827
My mom and dad packed it for me.

1945
01:04:53,828 --> 01:04:54,857
That was touching.

1946
01:04:54,858 --> 01:04:56,728
- My mom and dad. - Her parents packed her lunch.

1947
01:04:56,898 --> 01:04:59,098
- How cute! Her parents packed it. - Fried tofu rice balls?

1948
01:04:59,238 --> 01:05:00,898
My mom and dad made these.

1949
01:05:01,338 --> 01:05:02,538
- There's a letter! - Gosh!

1950
01:05:03,008 --> 01:05:04,108
Read it for us!

1951
01:05:04,608 --> 01:05:05,708
Read it for us!

1952
01:05:06,308 --> 01:05:07,607
Could you read it for me?

1953
01:05:07,608 --> 01:05:08,738
I'm going to tear up.

1954
01:05:10,078 --> 01:05:12,047
- Your mother wrote it? - Letters always make you cry.

1955
01:05:12,048 --> 01:05:13,117
Right.

1956
01:05:13,118 --> 01:05:15,948
"Today is the day of the exciting fall field day."

1957
01:05:16,988 --> 01:05:19,218
"We wondered what to pack for you as you asked for a packed lunch."

1958
01:05:19,618 --> 01:05:21,217
"The whole family got together and pleasantly thought about..."

1959
01:05:21,218 --> 01:05:22,628
- "what to make." - How cute.

1960
01:05:22,728 --> 01:05:24,057
- It must be her mother. - "We lived away from each other..."

1961
01:05:24,058 --> 01:05:25,357
"ever since you were young."

1962
01:05:25,358 --> 01:05:26,828
"We were never able to take good care of you."

1963
01:05:27,228 --> 01:05:29,398
"We are full of regret and sorrow based on that."

1964
01:05:29,828 --> 01:05:32,028
"We are very proud of you,"

1965
01:05:32,538 --> 01:05:33,967
"but you still are the most adorable youngest daughter in our family."

1966
01:05:33,968 --> 01:05:34,968
He sounds like a homeroom teacher.

1967
01:05:35,938 --> 01:05:37,168
She's a student he cherishes.

1968
01:05:37,508 --> 01:05:39,338
He's really harsh on Dae Ho.

1969
01:05:40,008 --> 01:05:41,278
But she's a student he adores.

1970
01:05:41,508 --> 01:05:42,807
- Dae Ho... - Lee Jung's mother...

1971
01:05:42,808 --> 01:05:44,108
is the president of the Parent-Teacher Association.

1972
01:05:45,848 --> 01:05:46,918
"Okay, Lee Jung."

1973
01:05:48,118 --> 01:05:50,018
"We wish that your outing today..."

1974
01:05:50,118 --> 01:05:52,458
"will become a precious memory."

1975
01:05:52,858 --> 01:05:54,688
"Enjoy your fall field day!"

1976
01:05:55,088 --> 01:05:56,728
"Love Mom, Dad, and your older brother."

1977
01:05:57,458 --> 01:06:00,357
Everyone, you must be aware of this.

1978
01:06:00,358 --> 01:06:03,768
It's Lee Jung's first time at a field day today.

1979
01:06:04,098 --> 01:06:05,998
- Really? - I've never been to one.

1980
01:06:06,538 --> 01:06:09,008
Then it must be your first time seeing food like Dae Ho's.

1981
01:06:09,408 --> 01:06:10,538
I've never seen that before.

1982
01:06:11,208 --> 01:06:14,178
- It's a first in Korea. - He deserves respect though.

1983
01:06:14,978 --> 01:06:17,147
(She keeps her first packed lunch and letter safe.)

1984
01:06:17,148 --> 01:06:18,748
Check out mine as well!

1985
01:06:18,978 --> 01:06:20,048
I brought raw gizzard shad.

1986
01:06:20,148 --> 01:06:22,388
- Really? - Raw gizzard shad?

1987
01:06:22,788 --> 01:06:24,147
I brought a raw gizzard shad salad.

1988
01:06:24,148 --> 01:06:25,718
Gosh, that's lovely.

1989
01:06:25,818 --> 01:06:26,918
Here.

1990
01:06:27,418 --> 01:06:28,457
Did you make it?

1991
01:06:28,458 --> 01:06:30,387
Dae Ho made quite a big reaction.

1992
01:06:30,388 --> 01:06:32,397
- His reaction was quite big. - Hold on.

1993
01:06:32,398 --> 01:06:33,657
Why are you being like that?

1994
01:06:33,658 --> 01:06:34,897
- Gosh. - That's amazing.

1995
01:06:34,898 --> 01:06:36,098
Gamtae abalone gimbap.

1996
01:06:36,298 --> 01:06:38,068
Gamtae abalone gimbap? Gosh!

1997
01:06:38,298 --> 01:06:40,367
- Ja Yeon put in a lot of effort. - She did.

1998
01:06:40,368 --> 01:06:42,407
- She put in a lot of effort. - Her food was great.

1999
01:06:42,408 --> 01:06:44,008
- Her food was great. - Her food was great.

2000
01:06:44,408 --> 01:06:45,708
What did you pack, MINHO?

2001
01:06:45,908 --> 01:06:48,807
I brought all of the side dishes my mom made for me.

2002
01:06:48,808 --> 01:06:50,078
You brought all of the side dishes?

2003
01:06:50,578 --> 01:06:52,107
- Since KEY was bringing the rice. - I brought his rice.

2004
01:06:52,108 --> 01:06:53,277
Ki Bum said he was going to bring the rice.

2005
01:06:53,278 --> 01:06:54,478
Dae Ho has a lot of rice too.

2006
01:06:54,918 --> 01:06:56,088
- Do you need some? - I'm fine.

2007
01:06:56,288 --> 01:06:57,418
Gosh.

2008
01:06:58,748 --> 01:06:59,858
What about you, Jae Hyeon?

2009
01:06:59,988 --> 01:07:03,057
I brought duck salad, meatballs,

2010
01:07:03,058 --> 01:07:04,227
- Did you make them yourself? - and beef bone soup.

2011
01:07:04,228 --> 01:07:05,558
- Beef bone soup? - Right.

2012
01:07:06,028 --> 01:07:07,457
- Did you make everything? - I did,

2013
01:07:07,458 --> 01:07:08,828
but the soup leaked.

2014
01:07:08,998 --> 01:07:10,628
There isn't a single drop left. All of the soup leaked.

2015
01:07:10,998 --> 01:07:12,568
All of the soup leaked.

2016
01:07:13,468 --> 01:07:15,538
What is that? It's my first time seeing that.

2017
01:07:16,268 --> 01:07:17,567
This is cold meat, Na Rae.

2018
01:07:17,568 --> 01:07:18,938
- What is that? - He said it was beef bone soup.

2019
01:07:19,138 --> 01:07:20,477
- Warm meat. - It's still warm.

2020
01:07:20,478 --> 01:07:22,238
This would be perfect for Bokdol.

2021
01:07:23,248 --> 01:07:24,307
- Give it to Bokdol. - Should I do that?

2022
01:07:24,308 --> 01:07:25,377
It wasn't seasoned, right?

2023
01:07:25,378 --> 01:07:26,447
It wasn't seasoned at all.

2024
01:07:26,448 --> 01:07:27,817
(Jae Hyeon's packed lunch can be shared with Bokdol.)

2025
01:07:27,818 --> 01:07:30,148
Dogs are often fed beef shank.

2026
01:07:30,848 --> 01:07:32,758
All of our packed lunches...

2027
01:07:33,088 --> 01:07:35,157
are completely different from each other.

2028
01:07:35,158 --> 01:07:36,458
- Right. - Right.

2029
01:07:36,658 --> 01:07:38,828
- That's what's fun about that. - That was why I enjoyed that time.

2030
01:07:38,998 --> 01:07:40,327
We all packed our lunches based on our characters.

2031
01:07:40,328 --> 01:07:41,498
Exactly.

2032
01:07:42,128 --> 01:07:43,427
What did you pack, Woo Il?

2033
01:07:43,428 --> 01:07:45,897
I packed the freshest things in my house.

2034
01:07:45,898 --> 01:07:47,598
- It wasn't something you had. - Right.

2035
01:07:47,898 --> 01:07:49,068
Canned food.

2036
01:07:49,168 --> 01:07:50,437
Canned food? That sounds fresh.

2037
01:07:50,438 --> 01:07:53,277
- The 3-minute instant curry. - The 3-minute instant curry.

2038
01:07:53,278 --> 01:07:54,408
There's also Spam.

2039
01:07:54,708 --> 01:07:56,208
Spam? That's a fresh meal.

2040
01:07:56,878 --> 01:07:58,748
Ju Seung's packed lunch looks really pretty!

2041
01:07:58,908 --> 01:08:01,847
- What's that? - My mom packed it in the morning.

2042
01:08:01,848 --> 01:08:04,047
- Oh, right. - His mother packed it for him.

2043
01:08:04,048 --> 01:08:05,188
Ms. Jeon Gwi Sim.

2044
01:08:05,248 --> 01:08:06,657
There are rice balls and fried tofu rice balls.

2045
01:08:06,658 --> 01:08:07,858
Why didn't my mom pack my lunch for me?

2046
01:08:07,988 --> 01:08:09,858
Your mother is a great cook.

2047
01:08:10,558 --> 01:08:11,628
What did you bring, Sung Hwan?

2048
01:08:11,688 --> 01:08:14,928
I brought a homemade burger.

2049
01:08:15,098 --> 01:08:18,468
It's a burger with shrimp, beef, and hash browns.

2050
01:08:19,598 --> 01:08:21,038
- I have one more thing. - What is it?

2051
01:08:21,498 --> 01:08:23,607
My best friend Ju Seung.

2052
01:08:23,608 --> 01:08:25,268
His mother packed this for me.

2053
01:08:25,438 --> 01:08:26,478
Fried tofu rice balls.

2054
01:08:26,878 --> 01:08:29,247
Ju Seung brought Sung Hwan's rice balls as well.

2055
01:08:29,248 --> 01:08:30,377
Right.

2056
01:08:30,378 --> 01:08:32,178
- You should eat all of this. - Right.

2057
01:08:33,278 --> 01:08:37,188
(Ju Seung's mother took great care of Sung Hwan from the past.)

2058
01:08:38,448 --> 01:08:40,257
There are always those friends.

2059
01:08:40,258 --> 01:08:41,817
Their mothers pack food for the friends as well.

2060
01:08:41,818 --> 01:08:43,028
(Feeling proud)

2061
01:08:43,728 --> 01:08:44,987
Did you not bring anything, CODE KUNST?

2062
01:08:44,988 --> 01:08:46,797
- Jang Woo! - The gimbap restaurant ladies...

2063
01:08:46,798 --> 01:08:47,997
packed these for me.

2064
01:08:47,998 --> 01:08:50,098
- They're like his mothers as well. - Right.

2065
01:08:50,228 --> 01:08:51,328
They are mothers of their own children.

2066
01:08:53,268 --> 01:08:54,698
(Walking around)

2067
01:08:54,898 --> 01:08:57,167
- Jang Woo! - Are you serious?

2068
01:08:57,168 --> 01:08:58,907
- Show us what you brought. - I felt so jealous.

2069
01:08:58,908 --> 01:08:59,977
- His wife made it for him. - Let's see.

2070
01:08:59,978 --> 01:09:01,477
- I'm jealous of that the most. - As I was on a diet,

2071
01:09:01,478 --> 01:09:03,278
she packed me some gimbap and side dishes.

2072
01:09:04,748 --> 01:09:06,277
- She made them? - Right.

2073
01:09:06,278 --> 01:09:07,347
- That's nice. - Gosh.

2074
01:09:07,348 --> 01:09:08,378
Right.

2075
01:09:08,478 --> 01:09:11,217
- The diet lunch packed with love. - Lunch packed with love.

2076
01:09:11,218 --> 01:09:12,718
- How is that diet food though? - Right.

2077
01:09:12,988 --> 01:09:14,057
The amount of food shows he's on a diet.

2078
01:09:14,058 --> 01:09:16,888
- That much means he's on a diet. - Right.

2079
01:09:17,088 --> 01:09:18,258
It's just like fasting for him.

2080
01:09:18,658 --> 01:09:19,798
It's Kang Yong's turn!

2081
01:09:20,358 --> 01:09:23,128
I brought the braised skate made by my mother.

2082
01:09:23,568 --> 01:09:24,827
The braised skate made by his mother!

2083
01:09:24,828 --> 01:09:25,897
- Gosh! - But...

2084
01:09:25,898 --> 01:09:27,967
- it was frozen. - You had it on the show.

2085
01:09:27,968 --> 01:09:29,238
Right. It's the braised skate.

2086
01:09:29,668 --> 01:09:31,938
- It wasn't fermented, right? - It wasn't fermented.

2087
01:09:33,938 --> 01:09:34,977
(His mother's braised skate that he had during his meals)

2088
01:09:34,978 --> 01:09:37,678
Everyone's lifestyle can be felt through the packed lunches.

2089
01:09:38,408 --> 01:09:39,547
What did you bring, Ji Hyeon?

2090
01:09:39,548 --> 01:09:42,247
I brought stir-fried octopus gimbap.

2091
01:09:42,248 --> 01:09:44,187
He also brought something that shows who he is.

2092
01:09:44,188 --> 01:09:45,817
- It reminds us of Mokpo. - Gosh.

2093
01:09:45,818 --> 01:09:46,988
I made this in the morning.

2094
01:09:48,588 --> 01:09:51,057
- Right. - It's so good.

2095
01:09:51,058 --> 01:09:53,028
- Thank you. - Thank you.

2096
01:09:53,128 --> 01:09:54,928
- Thank you. - It's good.

2097
01:09:55,028 --> 01:09:56,427
- Be careful. - It's unique.

2098
01:09:56,428 --> 01:09:57,597
That's what it's like.

2099
01:09:57,598 --> 01:09:58,898
Should I separate the crab for you?

2100
01:09:59,198 --> 01:10:00,198
Yes, please.

2101
01:10:00,268 --> 01:10:01,298
Pass it to me.

2102
01:10:01,938 --> 01:10:03,008
Thank you.

2103
01:10:03,408 --> 01:10:04,537
Ja Yeon is nice.

2104
01:10:04,538 --> 01:10:05,907
She separated the crabs for all of us.

2105
01:10:05,908 --> 01:10:07,908
- Ja Yeon did that? - Yes. Even for me.

2106
01:10:08,878 --> 01:10:10,008
Gosh!

2107
01:10:10,808 --> 01:10:11,808
(Sitting right next to the friend separating the crab for her)

2108
01:10:11,809 --> 01:10:14,518
Separate the middle like this.

2109
01:10:15,118 --> 01:10:16,488
Suck the meat out.

2110
01:10:16,818 --> 01:10:18,187
Thank you.

2111
01:10:18,188 --> 01:10:19,618
Check out Kian84's lunch.

2112
01:10:19,988 --> 01:10:22,828
(The Rainbow Club members all share the food together.)

2113
01:10:23,328 --> 01:10:25,087
Why didn't you bring a packed lunch?

2114
01:10:25,088 --> 01:10:26,357
Did you really not bring anything?

2115
01:10:26,358 --> 01:10:28,328
Moomoo didn't bring anything.

2116
01:10:28,558 --> 01:10:31,668
I packed a lot of food in case of people like him.

2117
01:10:32,028 --> 01:10:34,598
I thought that there would be more than enough food.

2118
01:10:36,068 --> 01:10:37,238
I fought with my mom.

2119
01:10:37,438 --> 01:10:39,438
- Gosh. - My mom didn't pack my lunch.

2120
01:10:39,538 --> 01:10:40,607
The icon of bad sons.

2121
01:10:40,608 --> 01:10:42,107
"My mom didn't pack my lunch."

2122
01:10:42,108 --> 01:10:43,548
(The icon of bad sons)

2123
01:10:43,678 --> 01:10:45,747
- Have some gimbap. - Thank you.

2124
01:10:45,748 --> 01:10:46,977
(Fortunately, Hyun Moo gets shared with food from everyone.)

2125
01:10:46,978 --> 01:10:48,047
Thank you!

2126
01:10:48,048 --> 01:10:49,318
(Fortunately, Hyun Moo gets shared with food from everyone.)

2127
01:10:49,648 --> 01:10:51,048
Try some of the skate.

2128
01:10:51,548 --> 01:10:53,558
It wasn't thawed enough though.

2129
01:10:55,188 --> 01:10:56,788
- I wanted to try the braised skate. - It's good.

2130
01:10:57,228 --> 01:10:59,197
Did you finish your kimchi fried rice, Kian84?

2131
01:10:59,198 --> 01:11:00,328
- Would you like to try some? - Yes.

2132
01:11:02,098 --> 01:11:03,898
- I'm really curious. - It's not that good.

2133
01:11:04,468 --> 01:11:06,038
- I'm still curious about your food. - Right.

2134
01:11:07,698 --> 01:11:09,868
I felt very grateful for MINHO.

2135
01:11:10,268 --> 01:11:13,308
No one was interested in my food, but he asked about mine first.

2136
01:11:13,908 --> 01:11:15,337
Did you finish it?

2137
01:11:15,338 --> 01:11:17,147
You didn't have much as well.

2138
01:11:17,148 --> 01:11:18,607
(I'll try Kian84's lunch as well.)

2139
01:11:18,608 --> 01:11:19,647
Could you pass me the wet wipes, Ja Yeon?

2140
01:11:19,648 --> 01:11:22,148
Was it made with the same recipe?

2141
01:11:22,248 --> 01:11:23,418
It was frozen.

2142
01:11:23,688 --> 01:11:25,548
- Give it a try. - What's this?

2143
01:11:25,818 --> 01:11:28,017
(Expectant)

2144
01:11:28,018 --> 01:11:29,117
Would anyone like some more of this?

2145
01:11:29,118 --> 01:11:31,857
I made it with the kimchi in the house.

2146
01:11:31,858 --> 01:11:33,428
It's actually fried rice this time.

2147
01:11:33,798 --> 01:11:36,227
It tastes a bit weird, doesn't it?

2148
01:11:36,228 --> 01:11:38,397
It looked like it would taste strong.

2149
01:11:38,398 --> 01:11:39,637
I thought it was going to be really salty.

2150
01:11:39,638 --> 01:11:41,268
More than how it tasted,

2151
01:11:41,368 --> 01:11:44,038
I loved how he showed interest in my food.

2152
01:11:44,368 --> 01:11:46,177
- It brought me to tears. - So you felt touched.

2153
01:11:46,178 --> 01:11:48,108
- I was asked twice. - I pretended to be cool about it.

2154
01:11:48,308 --> 01:11:50,547
I just indifferently said, "Do you want to try it?"

2155
01:11:50,548 --> 01:11:52,747
But inside, I was clapping like crazy.

2156
01:11:52,748 --> 01:11:54,577
We all felt grateful when a friend showed interest like that...

2157
01:11:54,578 --> 01:11:55,578
during our school days.

2158
01:11:55,579 --> 01:11:56,717
- Right. - "What did you bring?"

2159
01:11:56,718 --> 01:11:58,018
- That one sentence meant a lot. - Actually,

2160
01:11:58,248 --> 01:12:00,987
MINHO wasn't that interested in my food.

2161
01:12:00,988 --> 01:12:02,687
- He still asked about it though. - You could tell...

2162
01:12:02,688 --> 01:12:03,688
he did that on purpose.

2163
01:12:03,689 --> 01:12:05,457
When someone brings food that looks really good,

2164
01:12:05,458 --> 01:12:06,797
- everyone goes to that person. - They're all gathered there.

2165
01:12:06,798 --> 01:12:08,027
If no one asks about your food...

2166
01:12:08,028 --> 01:12:09,827
That guy is athletic and has a great character as well.

2167
01:12:09,828 --> 01:12:10,898
Right.

2168
01:12:11,798 --> 01:12:13,297
I can eat quickly.

2169
01:12:13,298 --> 01:12:14,898
(Shall I give it a try as well?)

2170
01:12:15,238 --> 01:12:16,767
It can be mixed with Dae Ho's food.

2171
01:12:16,768 --> 01:12:18,768
But mine tastes better.

2172
01:12:20,808 --> 01:12:22,078
You will never have this again.

2173
01:12:22,508 --> 01:12:24,608
What's wrong? It looks like it tastes strong.

2174
01:12:24,708 --> 01:12:26,417
- What was put into this? - Something is up.

2175
01:12:26,418 --> 01:12:28,277
(How does it taste for everyone to react that way?)

2176
01:12:28,278 --> 01:12:29,348
Gosh.

2177
01:12:30,448 --> 01:12:31,987
- Has it gone bad? - It hasn't gone bad.

2178
01:12:31,988 --> 01:12:33,558
- Even he won't ask for more. - It's clean.

2179
01:12:35,018 --> 01:12:36,228
Would you like some figs?

2180
01:12:36,528 --> 01:12:39,127
- The fig was really good. - That was really good.

2181
01:12:39,128 --> 01:12:40,997
They tasted different, didn't they? Jeolla Province figs are different.

2182
01:12:40,998 --> 01:12:42,998
Gosh, I'll have a fig.

2183
01:12:43,598 --> 01:12:45,398
Have some figs.

2184
01:12:45,568 --> 01:12:47,338
- There are figs? - There are figs?

2185
01:12:47,568 --> 01:12:48,867
- There are figs? - They're from Mokpo?

2186
01:12:48,868 --> 01:12:50,667
Gosh, there are figs!

2187
01:12:50,668 --> 01:12:52,267
- Rinse your mouth, Dae Ho. - Figs!

2188
01:12:52,268 --> 01:12:53,677
They sold a lot of these at Mokpo Station.

2189
01:12:53,678 --> 01:12:55,107
- Right. - It's so sweet!

2190
01:12:55,108 --> 01:12:56,348
You have to buy these.

2191
01:13:00,748 --> 01:13:02,147
Anyone want drinks?

2192
01:13:02,148 --> 01:13:03,917
You can't resist those.

2193
01:13:03,918 --> 01:13:05,048
- Right. - Definitely.

2194
01:13:05,688 --> 01:13:06,817
(Rinsing the mouth with a clean drink after the sweet figs)

2195
01:13:06,818 --> 01:13:08,457
Would you like one? Oh, you already have one?

2196
01:13:08,458 --> 01:13:09,688
Have some drinks.

2197
01:13:10,688 --> 01:13:12,457
- Thank you. - My goodness.

2198
01:13:12,458 --> 01:13:13,827
Thank you.

2199
01:13:13,828 --> 01:13:14,958
It's good.

2200
01:13:15,828 --> 01:13:19,167
It's a drink, but it's easy to drink instead of water.

2201
01:13:19,168 --> 01:13:21,398
- Right. It's really clean as well. - Right.

2202
01:13:22,038 --> 01:13:24,368
- This is good. - It's really clean.

2203
01:13:25,268 --> 01:13:26,508
You add soju to that.

2204
01:13:27,978 --> 01:13:29,038
It's a secret.

2205
01:13:30,448 --> 01:13:32,107
That's my two-percent secret.

2206
01:13:32,108 --> 01:13:33,648
(That's my little secret.)

2207
01:13:34,718 --> 01:13:36,448
To help digest the food...

2208
01:13:36,648 --> 01:13:37,688
What will we do now?

2209
01:13:37,888 --> 01:13:39,888
We can't move onto sports right away.

2210
01:13:40,558 --> 01:13:42,858
A congratulatory performance has been prepared.

2211
01:13:43,658 --> 01:13:44,928
Special guests are here.

2212
01:13:45,328 --> 01:13:46,827
- They are here just for all of you. - What?

2213
01:13:46,828 --> 01:13:48,728
Stay seated here.

2214
01:13:49,128 --> 01:13:51,498
The special guests will come out to perform.

2215
01:13:51,628 --> 01:13:53,468
What? Who could it be?

2216
01:13:53,698 --> 01:13:55,038
Today's...

2217
01:13:56,038 --> 01:13:57,468
congratulatory performance...

2218
01:13:57,708 --> 01:13:59,508
will be performed by...

2219
01:14:01,388 --> 01:14:03,058
(The stars of the congratulatory performance)

2220
01:14:03,558 --> 01:14:04,757
It's all of you!

2221
01:14:04,758 --> 01:14:05,788
- What? - Gosh.

2222
01:14:06,728 --> 01:14:08,027
It's all of you!

2223
01:14:08,028 --> 01:14:09,098
- What? - Gosh.

2224
01:14:09,858 --> 01:14:11,328
It's basically a talent show.

2225
01:14:11,798 --> 01:14:13,368
- Gosh, what? - Are you serious?

2226
01:14:14,068 --> 01:14:15,638
It's a talent show!

2227
01:14:17,468 --> 01:14:19,608
(Disappointed)

2228
01:14:19,868 --> 01:14:22,077
(Are there really no special guests?)

2229
01:14:22,078 --> 01:14:23,078
What is this?

2230
01:14:23,308 --> 01:14:26,047
(This sounds like fun.)

2231
01:14:26,048 --> 01:14:27,508
A talent show? What do I do?

2232
01:14:27,808 --> 01:14:28,848
Gosh.

2233
01:14:29,018 --> 01:14:30,817
You still should've known about it.

2234
01:14:30,818 --> 01:14:32,388
He did whatever he wanted.

2235
01:14:32,688 --> 01:14:34,147
So he came up with all of the ideas,

2236
01:14:34,148 --> 01:14:35,517
and you just did all the hard work.

2237
01:14:35,518 --> 01:14:37,257
That was the only thing he didn't tell me about.

2238
01:14:37,258 --> 01:14:38,317
I'm disappointed.

2239
01:14:38,318 --> 01:14:40,388
- It's more exciting as a surprise. - Right.

2240
01:14:41,428 --> 01:14:43,658
Get ready for the talent show.

2241
01:14:43,928 --> 01:14:45,468
For the opening performance...

2242
01:14:45,698 --> 01:14:46,727
Na Rae.

2243
01:14:46,728 --> 01:14:48,327
How are these thrown out?

2244
01:14:48,328 --> 01:14:49,637
- Here. - Please listen to me.

2245
01:14:49,638 --> 01:14:50,937
- That's general trash. - He prepared something.

2246
01:14:50,938 --> 01:14:52,407
Put everything down for now. CODE KUNST?

2247
01:14:52,408 --> 01:14:53,937
- Put it in here. - Put it down.

2248
01:14:53,938 --> 01:14:55,478
- No one is listening. - None of them listened.

2249
01:14:55,708 --> 01:14:56,937
Everyone, there will be...

2250
01:14:56,938 --> 01:14:58,278
Gosh.

2251
01:14:58,848 --> 01:15:00,007
There will be a performance.

2252
01:15:00,008 --> 01:15:01,748
- Fine. - Fine.

2253
01:15:02,848 --> 01:15:04,217
Get rid of the food trash later.

2254
01:15:04,218 --> 01:15:06,387
Didn't he prepare things for a magic show?

2255
01:15:06,388 --> 01:15:07,418
A magic show?

2256
01:15:07,788 --> 01:15:09,157
He must be taking things out from his bag.

2257
01:15:09,158 --> 01:15:10,757
No way. What are you saying?

2258
01:15:10,758 --> 01:15:11,817
All right.

2259
01:15:11,818 --> 01:15:12,958
(Rummaging)

2260
01:15:13,328 --> 01:15:14,357
What is that?

2261
01:15:14,358 --> 01:15:15,498
(A Rubik's Cube?)

2262
01:15:15,698 --> 01:15:17,357
- Is it really a magic show? - A Rubik's Cube?

2263
01:15:17,358 --> 01:15:18,898
He must've prepared a magic show.

2264
01:15:19,128 --> 01:15:20,928
(You're unbelievable.)

2265
01:15:21,098 --> 01:15:22,697
This is Jun Hyun Moo's Magic Show!

2266
01:15:22,698 --> 01:15:23,797
(Jun Hyun Moo's Magic Show)

2267
01:15:23,798 --> 01:15:25,408
- The Moogic Show. - The Moogic Show.

2268
01:15:25,708 --> 01:15:27,707
I went to a magic bar in Apgujeong...

2269
01:15:27,708 --> 01:15:29,437
- to learn this trick. - That's impressive.

2270
01:15:29,438 --> 01:15:30,677
I went to a magic bar in Apgujeong...

2271
01:15:30,678 --> 01:15:32,308
to learn that trick for four hours.

2272
01:15:32,548 --> 01:15:34,977
Do you know how to play with this?

2273
01:15:34,978 --> 01:15:36,448
- The Rubik's Cube. - Yes.

2274
01:15:36,978 --> 01:15:38,218
Your hand looks weird.

2275
01:15:39,218 --> 01:15:41,117
(Super awkward)

2276
01:15:41,118 --> 01:15:44,117
- His hand looks so weird. - That looks so suspicious.

2277
01:15:44,118 --> 01:15:45,787
Your hand looks so unnatural.

2278
01:15:45,788 --> 01:15:47,187
Your face is a bit weird!

2279
01:15:47,188 --> 01:15:48,528
My face was always weird.

2280
01:15:50,058 --> 01:15:51,497
How long does it take for you to solve this?

2281
01:15:51,498 --> 01:15:53,427
- Five minutes! - I don't know how to solve it!

2282
01:15:53,428 --> 01:15:54,498
I will...

2283
01:15:55,498 --> 01:15:56,737
solve it in less than two seconds.

2284
01:15:56,738 --> 01:15:58,067
- Come on! - Gosh!

2285
01:15:58,068 --> 01:15:59,237
- In less than two seconds. - Come on!

2286
01:15:59,238 --> 01:16:01,008
(Come on!)

2287
01:16:01,508 --> 01:16:04,138
(Singing)

2288
01:16:05,038 --> 01:16:06,447
(Excited)

2289
01:16:06,448 --> 01:16:07,607
Gosh, I'm so excited!

2290
01:16:07,608 --> 01:16:08,608
(Excited)

2291
01:16:09,918 --> 01:16:12,388
(Brace yourselves.)

2292
01:16:13,688 --> 01:16:15,287
Count to three for me.

2293
01:16:15,288 --> 01:16:17,258
- One, two, three! - One, two, three!

2294
